---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../../data';
---
<Base
  title="Telkomsel Orbit, Glen Hutajulu"
  description="A website revamp for a fixed wireless internet service."
  caseStudy
>
  <div class="wrap">

    <header class="case-head">
      <h1 class="h-wide">telkomsel orbit</h1>
      <p class="lede lede-wide mt-28">A website revamp for a fixed wireless internet service.</p>
    </header>

    <figure class="cover">
      <img class="img" src="/work/orbit/cover.webp" alt="Telkomsel Orbit website on a laptop beside two phones" width="2400" height="1280" decoding="async" fetchpriority="high">
    </figure>

    <section class="mt-24" aria-label="Project summary">
      <dl class="grid grid-260 summary">
        <div class="card-grey grain"><dt class="label">Problem</dt><dd class="small mt-10">Orbit needed a clearer website structure and simpler login, purchase and modem pairing flows to support its expanding digital ecosystem.</dd></div>
        <div class="card-grey grain"><dt class="label">Role and team</dt><dd class="small mt-10">UI/UX Designer at Aleph, working in a project team.</dd></div>
        <div class="card-grey grain"><dt class="label">Outcome</dt><dd class="small mt-10">Partially released between June and December 2024. The client did not share post-launch metrics.</dd></div>
        <div class="card-grey grain"><dt class="label">Timeline</dt><dd class="small mt-10">Mar 2024 – Nov 2024</dd></div>
      </dl>
    </section>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>Telkomsel Orbit is a fixed wireless internet service under Telkomsel. It set out on a major website revamp to improve the user experience and support its expanding digital ecosystem. I joined as a UI/UX Designer and supported the work across multiple touchpoints, from structural layout to system integration.</p>

      <h2 class="h-section mt-72">a clearer way through the website</h2>
      <p>I ran heuristic evaluations and user testing to simplify navigation and improve the content hierarchy across the Orbit website.</p>

      <h2 class="h-section mt-72">content people can follow</h2>
      <p>I revamped copy and visual structure for better readability, engagement and product clarity across key pages, including Home, Product and Support.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="band mt-lg" aria-label="Website pages">
    <div class="inner grid grid-260">
      <figure class="cell">
        <img class="crop ratio-3-5" src="/work/orbit/web-home.webp" alt="Telkomsel Orbit homepage with promotions, shortcuts and modem options" width="1440" height="4884" decoding="async" loading="lazy">
        <figcaption class="label mt-10">Homepage</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="cell">
        <img class="crop ratio-3-5" src="/work/orbit/web-modem.webp" alt="Modem product page with package options, specifications and features" width="1440" height="3010" decoding="async" loading="lazy">
        <figcaption class="label mt-10">Modem product page</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="cell">
        <img class="crop ratio-3-5" src="/work/orbit/web-halo.webp" alt="Halo Orbit program page with benefits, packages and activation guide" width="1440" height="6226" decoding="async" loading="lazy">
        <figcaption class="label mt-10">Halo Orbit program page</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="prose">
      <h2 class="h-section">getting a modem up and running</h2>
      <p>Working closely with the tech team, I redesigned and optimised the journeys for login, customer purchase and modem pairing via the website, to simplify onboarding for new users.</p>
      <p class="mt-14">Activation could start from a QR scan or a purchase email, with or without creating an account. Each path also covers what can go wrong: a modem that is not connected, an invalid field, a wrong OTP or a KTP that fails.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="split mt-md">
      <figure class="cell" style="flex: 347 1 347px">
        <img class="img" src="/work/orbit/flow-entry.webp" alt="Flow map of activation entry points, including QR scan, purchase email and activation without an account" width="1800" height="1038" decoding="async" loading="lazy" style="aspect-ratio: 1800 / 1038">
        <figcaption class="label mt-10">Activation entry points</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="cell" style="flex: 244 1 244px">
        <img class="img" src="/work/orbit/flow-prepaid.webp" alt="Flow map of prepaid activation on the web with its error states" width="1788" height="1464" decoding="async" loading="lazy" style="aspect-ratio: 1788 / 1464">
        <figcaption class="label mt-10">Prepaid activation and its error states</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2 class="h-section">one experience with mytelkomsel</h2>
      <p>With the product owners, I worked on a seamless cross-platform experience between the Orbit website and app and the MyTelkomsel app, particularly for account syncing and modem status visibility.</p>

      <h2 class="h-section mt-72">where it stands</h2>
      <p>The revamp was partially released between June and December 2024. The client did not share post-launch metrics, so I have no numbers to show. Internal feedback noted better synergy between Orbit's web platform and Telkomsel's broader digital ecosystem.</p>
      <p class="mt-40"><a href="/#work">Back to all work</a></p>
    </div>

  </div>
</Base>
